WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.021
Fine-tuning has driven much of the recent success
of language models,

00:00:04.101 --> 00:00:08.122
but it comes at a steep memory cost.

00:00:08.202 --> 00:00:12.223
Backpropagation must cache intermediate activations
and store gradients and optimizer states,

00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:16.324
which together can require up to twelve times the
memory of plain inference.

00:00:16.404 --> 00:00:20.426
As models scale into the tens of billions of parameters,

00:00:20.506 --> 00:00:24.527
this becomes the binding constraint.

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:28.628
Concretely,

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:32.729
a single eighty-gigabyte A100 GPU can run inference
on a thirty-billion-parameter model,

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:36.830
yet standard Adam fine-tuning on the same hardware
is limited to only a two-point-seven-billion-parameter model.
